{"status":"candidate","chosen_option":"streaming_simulation","assumptions":["Input is well-formed and contains n changes.","Python 3 integers can represent the supplied values and intermediate balances."],"observations":[{"statement":"The algorithm records the first negative balance and continues processing every change.","source_ids":["task"]},{"statement":"For public1 and public2, the expected result is 0.","source_ids":["public1","public2"]}],"artifact":{"code":"import sys

data = list(map(int, sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()))
n, balance = data[0], data[1]
first_negative = 0
for i in range(n):
    balance += data[i + 2]
    if first_negative == 0 and balance < 0:
        first_negative = i + 1
print(first_negative)"}}
